{"type":"message","id":"faf241b1","parentId":"db08259c","timestamp":"2026-06-12T12:05:43.789Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"read_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.cursor/plans/fix_drive_docx_image_missing_ef4913ba.plan.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":382,"output":43,"cacheRead":13140,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":13565,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781265942622,"responseId":"F_YravGFGOiy694PncrXiAk"}}
{"type":"message","id":"cb05f274","parentId":"faf241b1","timestamp":"2026-06-12T12:05:43.844Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"read_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: Fix Drive Docx Image Missing\noverview: Replicate the WP publisher's proven readlink -f + size-check pattern in the Publisher SOUL as a mandatory bash step before embedding, and add --resource-path /tmp to the pandoc command as a hard safety net. The LLM must execute real bash to resolve the path — not just think about it — exactly mirroring what publish.sh already does reliably for WordPress.\ntodos:\n  - id: publisher-soul-resolve-step\n    content: \"Replace Step 1 in workspace-publisher/SOUL.md with a WP-style two-phase approach: (a) mandatory bash step that runs readlink -f, stat size-check > 51200 bytes, and sets EFFECTIVE_IMAGE — same logic as publish.sh lines 363-366 and 369-370; (b) printf command uses $EFFECTIVE_IMAGE (the resolved real path) not $FEATURE_JPG.\"\n    status: completed\n  - id: publisher-soul-pandoc\n    content: Add --resource-path /tmp to the pandoc command in workspace-publisher/SOUL.md Step 2 as a safety net.\n    status: completed\nisProject: false\n---\n\n# Fix: Image Missing in Google Drive Docx\n\n## Root cause (confirmed by test)\n\nWordPress works because `publish.sh` (lines 363–400) uses the exact pattern:\n\n```bash\nEFFECTIVE_IMAGE=\"$IMAGE_PATH\"\nif [ -f \"$IMAGE_PATH\" ]; then\n  EFFECTIVE_IMAGE=$(readlink -f \"$IMAGE_PATH\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"$IMAGE_PATH\")\nfi\nif [ -f \"$EFFECTIVE_IMAGE\" ]; then\n  FILE_SIZE=$(stat -c%s \"$EFFECTIVE_IMAGE\" 2>/dev/null || ...)\n  if [ \"$FILE_SIZE\" -gt 51200 ]; then\n    # use EFFECTIVE_IMAGE for upload\n  fi\nfi\n```\n\nIt resolves the symlink to a real absolute path, size-checks it, then uploads the real bytes. The path is never relative, never guessed.\n\nThe Publisher (Drive) SOUL does NOT do this. Its Step 1 is:\n\n```bash\nprintf '![Feature Image](%s)\\n\\n' \"$FEATURE_JPG\" | cat - \"$ARTICLE_MD\" > \"$WITH_IMAGE_MD\"\n```\n\nThe LLM is responsible for substituting `$FEATURE_JPG` correctly. When it substitutes a **relative** filename (`crypto-feature.jpg` instead of `/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg`), pandoc silently warns:\n\n```\n[WARNING] Could not fetch resource crypto-feature.jpg: replacing image with description\n```\n\nPandoc exits 0 — no error — but the docx contains zero embedded media. Drive upload succeeds with a broken docx. WordPress is immune because its script never lets a relative path through.\n\n**All three cases tested and confirmed:**\n- `readlink -f` resolved real path → docx has `word/media/rId20.jpg` — image embedded\n- Relative path, no `--resource-path` → zero media files, image gone\n- Relative path + `--resource-path /tmp` → docx has `word/media/rId20.jpg` — image embedded\n\n## Files to change\n\n### 1. MODIFY: [`workspace-publisher/SOUL.md`](workspace-publisher/SOUL.md)\n\n**Replace Step 1** with a WP-style two-phase approach:\n\n```markdown\n### Step 1: Resolve the image path and embed\n\nFirst, resolve the real image path exactly as the WordPress script does — run this bash command:\n\n```bash\nEFFECTIVE_IMAGE=\"$FEATURE_JPG\"\nif [ -f \"$FEATURE_JPG\" ]; then\n  EFFECTIVE_IMAGE=$(readlink -f \"$FEATURE_JPG\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"$FEATURE_JPG\")\nfi\nFILE_SIZE=$(stat -c%s \"$EFFECTIVE_IMAGE\" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)\necho \"Feature image: $EFFECTIVE_IMAGE ($FILE_SIZE bytes)\"\n```\n\nIf `$FILE_SIZE` is greater than 51200 (50 KB), embed the image using the resolved real path:\n\n```bash\nprintf '![Feature Image](%s)\\n\\n' \"$EFFECTIVE_IMAGE\" | cat - \"$ARTICLE_MD\" > \"$WITH_IMAGE_MD\"\n```\n\nIf the image is missing or too small, skip embedding and copy the plain article:\n\n```bash\ncp \"$ARTICLE_MD\" \"$WITH_IMAGE_MD\"\n```\n```\n\nThe critical change: `$EFFECTIVE_IMAGE` (from `readlink -f`) replaces `$FEATURE_JPG` in the printf command. This is a bash-enforced resolved path — the LLM cannot accidentally use a relative name or an unresolved symlink variable, because the bash command already ran and set `EFFECTIVE_IMAGE` to the real absolute path.\n\n**Update Step 2** — add `--resource-path /tmp` as hard safety net:\n\n```bash\npandoc \"$WITH_IMAGE_MD\" -o \"$ARTICLE_DOCX\" --standalone --resource-path /tmp\n```\n\nIf any relative path somehow survives to this point, pandoc finds it via the `/tmp/` symlinks.\n\n**These are the only two changes.** One file, no new scripts, no workflow changes.\n\n## Why this is better than a thinking block\n\nA `<thinking>` block is an instruction to the LLM to think before acting — it can still be ignored or skipped. The WP-style approach forces a concrete bash execution step. The LLM cannot use a relative path because `$EFFECTIVE_IMAGE` is already set to the resolved real path by the time it reaches the printf command. This mirrors exactly how `publish.sh` prevents the same class of failure on the WP side.\n\n## What is NOT changed\n\n- Publisher SOUL Steps 3 and 4 (Drive upload) — untouched\n- `publish.sh` (WP script) — already works correctly, untouched\n- Orchestrator SOUL — untouched\n- `verify_artifacts.py` — untouched\n- `init_run.sh`, `switch_iteration.sh` — untouched\n- `generate.sh`, Creator/Pixel SOUL — untouched\n- All other agents and scripts — untouched\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1781265943844}}
{"type":"message","id":"072cd0e5","parentId":"cb05f274","timestamp":"2026-06-12T12:05:45.201Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"read_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/save_google_drive_json.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":3631,"output":41,"cacheRead":11342,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15014,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781265943845,"responseId":"GPYraozqKZTO694PxaqQ6QE"}}
{"type":"message","id":"6ed290f7","parentId":"072cd0e5","timestamp":"2026-06-12T12:05:45.238Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"read_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nsave_google_drive_json.py — Persist Google Drive upload metadata to the run bundle.\n\nUsage:\n    python3 save_google_drive_json.py \\\n        --manifest /path/to/manifest.json \\\n        --json '{\"webViewLink\":\"https://...\"}' \n\n    python3 save_google_drive_json.py \\\n        --manifest /path/to/manifest.json \\\n        --web-view-link \"https://docs.google.com/...\"\n\nExit 0 + prints DRIVE_JSON_SAVED: <path>\nExit 1 + prints DRIVE_JSON_ERROR: <reason>\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\n\n\ndef extract_web_view_link(text: str) -> str | None:\n    text = text.strip()\n    if not text:\n        return None\n    try:\n        data = json.loads(text)\n        if isinstance(data, dict):\n            link = data.get(\"webViewLink\") or data.get(\"web_view_link\") or data.get(\"url\")\n            if link:\n                return str(link).strip()\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        pass\n    match = re.search(r\"https://docs\\.google\\.com/[^\\s\\\"'<>]+\", text)\n    if match:\n        return match.group(0).rstrip(\".,)\")\n    return None\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument(\"--manifest\", required=True)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--json\", default=\"\", help=\"Raw JSON from gog drive upload\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--web-view-link\", default=\"\", help=\"Direct Google Doc URL\")\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    manifest_path = os.path.realpath(args.manifest)\n    if not os.path.isfile(manifest_path):\n        print(f\"DRIVE_JSON_ERROR: manifest not found: {manifest_path}\")\n        return 1\n\n    try:\n        with open(manifest_path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            manifest = json.load(f)\n    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError) as e:\n        print(f\"DRIVE_JSON_ERROR: cannot read manifest: {e}\")\n        return 1\n\n    run_dir = manifest.get(\"run_dir\") or \"\"\n    if not run_dir:\n        print(\"DRIVE_JSON_ERROR: manifest missing run_dir\")\n        return 1\n\n    web_view_link = (args.web_view_link or \"\").strip()\n    payload: dict = {}\n\n    raw_json = (args.json or \"\").strip()\n    if raw_json:\n        try:\n            parsed = json.loads(raw_json)\n            if isinstance(parsed, dict):\n                payload = parsed\n                if not web_view_link:\n                    web_view_link = str(\n                        parsed.get(\"webViewLink\") or parsed.get(\"web_view_link\") or \"\"\n                    ).strip()\n        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n            link = extract_web_view_link(raw_json)\n            if link:\n                web_view_link = link\n\n    if not web_view_link:\n        link = extract_web_view_link(raw_json)\n        if link:\n            web_view_link = link\n\n    if not web_view_link:\n        print(\"DRIVE_JSON_ERROR: no webViewLink found in input\")\n        return 1\n\n    payload.setdefault(\"webViewLink\", web_view_link)\n    payload[\"web_view_link\"] = web_view_link\n\n    out_dir = os.path.join(run_dir, \"publish\")\n    os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n    out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, \"google-drive.json\")\n\n    try:\n        with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            json.dump(payload, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n            f.write(\"\\n\")\n    except OSError as e:\n        print(f\"DRIVE_JSON_ERROR: cannot write {out_path}: {e}\")\n        return 1\n\n    print(f\"DRIVE_JSON_SAVED: {out_path}\")\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1781265945238}}
